                        "entry_id": "51f4c58e-8823-3e96-821d-468c4ce2b82f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The area beside a pool."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "956bb5ba-e832-4aef-8cd0-f02cc319f821",
                                "sense_id": "c938e938-745d-3718-b978-5a889573208f",
                                "text": "[…] as it is evident the poet alludes to a trout that has caught sight of the angler, and safe he is, at least pro tem., as our pupils who first frighten the fish by walking down a poolside, and then fish up it, will find to their cost."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a242e2ee-143c-4e37-8b44-41ed84a54e3c",
                                "sense_id": "c938e938-745d-3718-b978-5a889573208f",
                                "text": "I am afraid the site, by a poolside where no Dane's boat could have got, negatives this, until other stations by navigable streams — the nearest is two miles to the east of the present site — are discovered."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fb4ef59-2b69-4649-9564-1643a19ab5ea",
                                "sense_id": "c938e938-745d-3718-b978-5a889573208f",
                                "text": "A ringing cell phone was no stranger at hotel poolsides, the upscale, plastic-dominated resort he'd been in for the past week being no exception."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
